{
  "source": "scripts/color-taylor-script-cut-05.md",
  "wpm": 150,
  "gaps": {
    "line": 0.5,
    "paragraph": 1.2,
    "beat": 2.5
  },
  "lead": 3,
  "tail": 3,
  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "1.1",
      "beat": 1,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "Hey, I'm Taylor.",
      "start": 3,
      "end": 4.2,
      "gapBefore": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "1.1",
      "beat": 1,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "I'm a real person.",
      "start": 4.7,
      "end": 6.3,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "1.2",
      "beat": 1,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "I'm also a user experience and product designer,",
      "start": 6.8,
      "end": 10,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "1.3",
      "beat": 1,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "and I'd like to show you something I've been working on.",
      "start": 10.5,
      "end": 14.9,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "1.4",
      "beat": 1,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "It's called Color Taylor.",
      "start": 15.4,
      "end": 17,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "1.5",
      "beat": 1,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "I'll just move myself out of the way, for now.",
      "start": 18.2,
      "end": 22.2,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "2.1",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "I used to struggle with picking colors using RGB.",
      "start": 24.7,
      "end": 28.3,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.2",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "In time, I found hue and saturation models were helpful for dialing in the colors I want.",
      "start": 28.8,
      "end": 35.6,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.3",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "Let's say I have this turquoise,",
      "start": 36.8,
      "end": 39.2,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "2.4",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "but I want to get it to teal,",
      "start": 39.7,
      "end": 42.9,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.5",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "which is a harmonious, but darker color.",
      "start": 43.4,
      "end": 46.2,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.6",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 6,
      "text": "How do I dial that into RGB?",
      "start": 46.7,
      "end": 49.5,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.7",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 7,
      "text": "I think I need to lower the red",
      "start": 50.7,
      "end": 53.9,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "2.8",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 8,
      "text": "and the blue,",
      "start": 54.4,
      "end": 55.6,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.9",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 9,
      "text": "but how much do I change the RGB before I stray too far from my source?",
      "start": 56.8,
      "end": 63.2,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "2.10",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 10,
      "text": "Once I understood how hue models and RGB work together,",
      "start": 64.4,
      "end": 68.4,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "2.11",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 11,
      "text": "I could more confidently understand how colors were constructed.",
      "start": 68.9,
      "end": 72.5,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.12",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 12,
      "text": "There, that's teal.",
      "start": 73.7,
      "end": 74.9,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "2.13",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 13,
      "text": "Our focus for this presentation will be on hue, saturation, and brightness.",
      "start": 76.1,
      "end": 80.9,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "2.14",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 14,
      "text": "The app supports HSL as well, so you can use what's familiar to you.",
      "start": 81.4,
      "end": 87,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.15",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 15,
      "text": "Color Taylor is meant to be a playground and educational tool for how RGB and HSB work together.",
      "start": 88.2,
      "end": 95.4,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "2.16",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 16,
      "text": "You see the relationships in real time,",
      "start": 95.9,
      "end": 98.7,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.17",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 17,
      "text": "which can strengthen your understanding of how colors work on displays.",
      "start": 99.2,
      "end": 103.6,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "3.1",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "The color editor on the right side should be familiar to most people who have worked with creative tools.",
      "start": 106.1,
      "end": 113.7,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "3.2",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "The hexagon on the left is a different way of displaying the same information.",
      "start": 114.9,
      "end": 120.5,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.3",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "Around the hexagon we have the Hue,",
      "start": 121.7,
      "end": 124.5,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.4",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "which is an angle that ranges from 0",
      "start": 125,
      "end": 128.2,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "3.5",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "to 360 degrees.",
      "start": 128.7,
      "end": 129.9,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "3.6",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 6,
      "text": "Red is 0...",
      "start": 131.1,
      "end": 132.3,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.7",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 7,
      "text": "green is 120...",
      "start": 133.5,
      "end": 134.7,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.8",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 8,
      "text": "and blue is 240.",
      "start": 135.9,
      "end": 137.5,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.9",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 9,
      "text": "By laying the primary colors out like this,",
      "start": 138.7,
      "end": 141.9,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.10",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 10,
      "text": "we can visualize how RGB values determine a color's hue.",
      "start": 142.4,
      "end": 146.4,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "3.11",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 11,
      "text": "Drag the handles around and you see how",
      "start": 147.6,
      "end": 150.8,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.12",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 12,
      "text": "red, green, and blue combine to make the color.",
      "start": 151.3,
      "end": 154.9,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "3.13",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 13,
      "text": "You'll notice, between each of the primary colors we see combinations:",
      "start": 156.1,
      "end": 160.5,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.14",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 14,
      "text": "yellow, which is red and green combined;",
      "start": 161.7,
      "end": 164.5,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.15",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 15,
      "text": "cyan, which is green and blue combined;",
      "start": 165.7,
      "end": 168.5,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.16",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 16,
      "text": "and magenta, which is blue and red combined.",
      "start": 169.7,
      "end": 172.9,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "4.1",
      "beat": 4,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "Let's use an orangey color as a reference point,",
      "start": 175.4,
      "end": 179,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "4.2",
      "beat": 4,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "Around 30 degrees we'll always have this warm tone between red and yellow.",
      "start": 180.2,
      "end": 185.4,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "4.3",
      "beat": 4,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "At the highest saturation and brightness the color will be a combination of",
      "start": 186.6,
      "end": 191.8,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "4.4",
      "beat": 4,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "2 parts red,",
      "start": 192.3,
      "end": 193.5,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "4.5",
      "beat": 4,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "1 part green,",
      "start": 194,
      "end": 195.2,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "4.6",
      "beat": 4,
      "line": 6,
      "text": "0 parts blue.",
      "start": 195.7,
      "end": 196.9,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "5.1",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "Saturation determines how colorful a color is.",
      "start": 199.4,
      "end": 202.2,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "5.2",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "100% saturation, like what we have here,",
      "start": 203.4,
      "end": 206.2,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "5.3",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "means the highest and lowest values are as far apart as they can be.",
      "start": 206.7,
      "end": 212.3,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "5.4",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "Desaturating reduces the range between red, green, and blue proportionally.",
      "start": 213.5,
      "end": 217.5,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "5.5",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "When all three values are equal, there's no saturation, and you're left with gray.",
      "start": 218.7,
      "end": 224.3,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "5.6",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 6,
      "text": "Adding saturation increases the range between values.",
      "start": 225.5,
      "end": 228.3,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "5.7",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 7,
      "text": "Saturation scales off the highest value.",
      "start": 229.5,
      "end": 231.9,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "5.8",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 8,
      "text": "For this orange, it's red, which holds still.",
      "start": 232.4,
      "end": 235.6,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "5.9",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 9,
      "text": "Green and blue move toward red or away from it",
      "start": 236.8,
      "end": 240.8,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "5.10",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 10,
      "text": "as we move the saturation slider.",
      "start": 241.3,
      "end": 243.7,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "5.11",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 11,
      "text": "Notice that the hue didn't change, only the range between RGB values changed.",
      "start": 244.9,
      "end": 250.1,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "5.12",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 12,
      "text": "We're still at 30, which is the same orangey source color we started with.",
      "start": 250.6,
      "end": 256.2,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "6.1",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "Brightness determines how light or dark a color is.",
      "start": 258.7,
      "end": 262.3,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "6.2",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "The highest RGB value sets the brightness.",
      "start": 263.5,
      "end": 266.3,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "6.3",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "As we adjust the brightness,",
      "start": 267.5,
      "end": 269.5,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "6.4",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "the hue and saturation are maintained.",
      "start": 270,
      "end": 272.4,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "6.5",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "This is done by scaling the RGB values proportionally to each other.",
      "start": 272.9,
      "end": 277.7,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "6.6",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 6,
      "text": "Brightness scales off of zero.",
      "start": 278.9,
      "end": 280.9,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "6.7",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 7,
      "text": "At 100% brightness the hexagon is at its largest.",
      "start": 282.1,
      "end": 285.7,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "6.8",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 8,
      "text": "As we lower it, the hexagon contracts,",
      "start": 286.2,
      "end": 289,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "6.9",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 9,
      "text": "and the red, green, and blue stems shorten with it,",
      "start": 289.5,
      "end": 293.5,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "6.10",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 10,
      "text": "keeping the same angles and proportions.",
      "start": 294,
      "end": 296.4,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "6.11",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 11,
      "text": "Notice we stay at that same 30 degree orangey color while moving the brightness.",
      "start": 296.9,
      "end": 302.5,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "7.1",
      "beat": 7,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "We'll use the swatches section to show how we can use HSB to set six different variations of the same hue.",
      "start": 305,
      "end": 313.4,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "7.2",
      "beat": 7,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "We can use HSB to come up with a bright desaturated orange,",
      "start": 314.6,
      "end": 319.4,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "7.3",
      "beat": 7,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "then go down the scale until we have a dark vibrant variant.",
      "start": 319.9,
      "end": 324.7,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "7.4",
      "beat": 7,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "This is hinting at what a design system might do.",
      "start": 325.9,
      "end": 329.9,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "8.1",
      "beat": 8,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "We've been exploring the playground,",
      "start": 332.4,
      "end": 334.4,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "8.2",
      "beat": 8,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "but if you want the classroom perspective,",
      "start": 334.9,
      "end": 337.7,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "8.3",
      "beat": 8,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "check out the equations section.",
      "start": 338.2,
      "end": 340.2,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "8.4",
      "beat": 8,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "It shows the math behind",
      "start": 341.4,
      "end": 343.4,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "8.5",
      "beat": 8,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "hue,",
      "start": 343.9,
      "end": 344.3,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "8.6",
      "beat": 8,
      "line": 6,
      "text": "saturation,",
      "start": 344.8,
      "end": 345.2,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "8.7",
      "beat": 8,
      "line": 7,
      "text": "brightness,",
      "start": 345.7,
      "end": 346.1,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "8.8",
      "beat": 8,
      "line": 8,
      "text": "as well as how Hex and normalized colors are calculated.",
      "start": 347.3,
      "end": 351.3,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "9.1",
      "beat": 9,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "Now we can move on to the demo.",
      "start": 353.8,
      "end": 357,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "10.1",
      "beat": 10,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "Start with the sliders and controls you already know.",
      "start": 359.5,
      "end": 363.1,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "10.2",
      "beat": 10,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "Moving one slider will highlight every other slider it affects.",
      "start": 364.3,
      "end": 368.3,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "10.3",
      "beat": 10,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "Click the droplet button to switch between Source or Mixed colored sliders.",
      "start": 369.5,
      "end": 374.3,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "10.4",
      "beat": 10,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "Click the tags button to show HTML colors on the hexagon.",
      "start": 375.5,
      "end": 379.9,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "10.5",
      "beat": 10,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "Drag a handle on the hexagon and watch the RGB and HSB sliders follow.",
      "start": 381.1,
      "end": 386.7,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "10.6",
      "beat": 10,
      "line": 6,
      "text": "Have fun exploring and learning about different color models.",
      "start": 387.9,
      "end": 391.5,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "11.1",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "If you use Figma, I've also made a Color Taylor plugin that you might like to check out.",
      "start": 394,
      "end": 401.2,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "11.2",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "That's Color Taylor!",
      "start": 402.4,
      "end": 403.6,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "11.3",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "Go play with it, and I hope it helps you see the relationship between RGB and HSB in a different light.",
      "start": 404.1,
      "end": 412.5,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "11.4",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "If it's useful, I'd like to hear from you.",
      "start": 413.7,
      "end": 417.3,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "11.4",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "Questions and feedback are welcome.",
      "start": 417.8,
      "end": 419.8,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "11.5",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "Thanks for watching.",
      "start": 421,
      "end": 422.2,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "11.5",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "See ya.",
      "start": 422.7,
      "end": 423.5,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    }
  ],
